To create a v switch bridge in the Ubuntu operating system, we need to follow these steps:

1. Create a new bridge device.
2. Configuration the bridge device.
3. Add the primary interface to the bridge.
4. Configuration the gateway to have Internet access.
5. Move the IP address from the main interface to the bridge.

Here is the bash script that will perform these steps:

```bash
# Step 1: Create a new bridge device
# The bridge device will be named "bridge0"
 bridg e0 -i eth0 -o eth2 -b 10.0.1.1 -w eth2 -m 10.0.1.2 -p 10.0.1.3 -l 10.0.1.4 -s 10.0.1.5 -r 10.0.1.6 -d 10.0.1.7 -t 10.0.1.8 -v 10.0.1.9 -w 10.0.1.10 -m 10.0.1.11 -p 10.0.1.12 -l 10.0.1.13 -s 10.0.1.14 -r 10.0.1.15 -d 10.0.1.16 -t 10.0.1.17 -v 10.0.1.18 -w 10.0.1.19 -m 10.0.1.20 -p bowls :";
